  "outcome": "resolved",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, I checked your mailbox and it's 99.4% full, which is why Outlook keeps warning you and some emails won't send. Sending stops completely once it reaches 100%. Here's how to free up space:\n\n1. Empty your Deleted Items and Junk Email folders. Right-click each folder and choose Empty Folder.\n2. In your Inbox and Sent Items, sort by size. Then delete large emails you don't need, or save their attachments to OneDrive and delete the emails.\n3. If you need to keep older mail, turn on Online Archive and move mail older than a year into it. This frees space without losing anything.\n\nIt can take up to an hour for the mailbox to update afterwards. After that, sending should work again and the warnings should stop. If you're still above 95% after cleaning up, or your job needs you to keep more mail than this, reply here. We can look at a larger mailbox, but that needs your manager's approval.",
  "internal_note": "Followed KB-010. Looked up the user (Mei Chen, id 9, Operations Logistics Analyst): the account is active and not locked. Mailbox is using 50,890 of 51,200 MB (99.4%), which explains the warnings and the failed sends. I gave the user the self-service cleanup steps: empty Deleted Items and Junk, sort by size and move attachments to OneDrive, and turn on Online Archive for mail older than a year. No technician action needed right now. Escalate per KB-010 only if the mailbox is still over 95% after cleanup and the role justifies a bigger quota (needs manager approval).",
